Z||000000||Swany||05-29-2001||12:53 AM||||I just bought my first Fiero 2 days ago.. 86 Fiero GT .. and I love the car.. <P>I've been going through tring to fix the few problems I've found,, and am having trouble figureing out this one.. <P>When I turn on the headlights, the dash lights don't come on.. <P>They did come on.. the first time I turned on the headlights, they came on after about 1 min,.. the second time, it took about 5 mins,, and I haven't seen them since.. <P>The dimmer switch has them turned up, of course, and the switch does turn on the interior light.. <P>I've checked the fuse, looked fine, switched it just in case, same prob.. <P>Anyone have any ideas? <P>I'm really new to this car, but plan on doing most of the work myself, only way to really learn.. <P>Thanks<P>Swany||||reg||1
Z||000001||Vader||05-29-2001||01:00 AM||||There is a dimmer control module in the instrument cluster.  The dimmer control on teh light switch array doesn't control the lamps directly.  Check the output transistor on this control and the dimmer potentiometer on the switch.<P>------------------<BR>"<I>Let the bodies hit the floor!</I>"||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||05-29-2001||01:41 PM||||there are more detailed notes about the dimmer in my cave... sounds like the transistor socket isn't making a good connection (Very likely) or the transistor may be bad(Not so likely).<P>Fiero store has a picture of what the transistor assembly looks like...||||reg||1
Z||000003||84Bill||05-29-2001||01:46 PM||||Since no one else has said it<BR>WELCOME to the Forum  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/sig.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||Swany||05-29-2001||03:00 PM||||Thanks guys, I'm gonna go through it tonight and check it out.. would be nice to see how much I'm speeding at night :-)<P>the way it was coming on and off, it sounded like a connection is lose to me, but didn't know where to start.. <P>noticed a new prob today, I'm hoping isn't going to be to big,, I'm leaking a little oil.. but it looks like the dealership over filled it.. so I'm thinking a good oil change is in order. .<P>Thanks again.. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Swany||05-30-2001||07:59 PM||||well, after checking the connection on the transister several times, its still not working.. the connections were not coroded, and everything looked normal.. I'm going to look into it a little deeper this weekend. check it out with a volt meter, see if the prob is pointing to the switch , transister or a bad ground.. <P>oh. ogre, I like your site, thanks for pointing that out, I went through my hayes manual for bout 20 mins looking for where that transister was at.. before I went back online .. :-)<p>[This message has been edited by Swany (edited 05-30-2001).]||||reg||1
